<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shia Islam</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Shia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shia <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> is one of the two main branches of Islam, whose adherents hold that leadership of the community belonged to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-ibn-abi-talib">Ali ibn Abi Talib</a> and his descendants. It emerged from the succession disputes described in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> profiles. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a> made Twelver Shia Islam the state religion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, and the Zand and Ayyubid profiles also refer to it.</p></div>
